@cc ===========================================================================
@cc CHATUI:MODE - build the NDCHAT full-screen main window on D100.
@cc
@cc   @MODE CHATUI:MODE,,
@cc
@cc Needs these under SYSTEM, all of which TESTUI already put there:
@cc
@cc   CHATUI:PLNC   the source
@cc   SCREEN:SYMB   the PLANC-SCREEN-H interface, $INCLUDEd by the source
@cc   INTRF1B:BRF   the PLANC-SCREEN-H 1-bank runtime
@cc   VTMR:BRF      VTM routines - VTMR supplies eight of the nine VT* entries
@cc   VTMDATA:BRF
@cc   VTMARR:BRF    says "Redefinition ... VTI4DDB" and that is harmless
@cc
@cc VTMCPOS and VTMCPAR are NOT loaded - VTMR already defines both, and loading
@cc them answers "Redefinition. First applies VTCPOS".
@cc
@cc READ WHAT LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED PRINTS. An undefined entry does NOT fail
@cc the build: BRF-LINKER still writes a runnable CHATUI:PROG which then
@cc misbehaves in ways that look like a bug in the program.
@cc
@cc AND READ THE LISTING, not the screen. The "0 DIAGNOSTICS" that stays visible
@cc belongs to the SECOND pass and sits happily under a COMPILE that had three
@cc errors.
@cc ===========================================================================
@DELETE-FILE CHATUI:PROG
@DELETE-FILE CHATUI:LIST
@DELETE-FILE CHATUI:BRF
@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE CHATUI:PLNC,"CHATUI:LIST","CHATUI"
EXIT
@BRF-LINKER-C01
PROGRAM-FILE "CHATUI"
LOAD CHATUI
LIBRARY-MODE ON
LOAD INTRF1B
LOAD VTMR
LOAD VTMDATA
LOAD VTMARR
LOAD MON-CALL-1B-A00
LOAD PLANC-1BANK-F00
LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED
EXIT
@cc ===========================================================================
@cc Built CHATUI:PROG. Run it with @CHATUI
@cc
@cc   ESC        leave
@cc   PAGE UP    page back through the scrollback
@cc   PAGE DOWN  page forward, and to the bottom returns to LIVE
@cc   RETURN     send what is typed - and always returns to LIVE
@cc
@cc A line arrives by itself every five seconds so there is something to page.
@cc ===========================================================================
